# xdiff_exit_halt.hls — the Stage 133 cross-impl table: the deliberate
# halt class. The program exits with 7 after printing one line. The
# interpreter and the native build exit 7; the wasm alpha halts every
# exit(N) through the same `unreachable` trap that panics use (its
# documented alpha convention: a visible halt beats a silent wrong
# answer — the CODE is not propagated, only the HALT is). The suite's
# halt law therefore expects `halt-gap` here: every backend halts,
# the hosted pair agrees on 7, wasm traps. A backend that prints
# "after" instead of halting rings as a divergence — that was the
# deep-scan-20 bug class, and this fixture keeps it un-regressable.
fn main() uses IO, Exit {
    println("halting")
    exit(7)
    println("after")
}
